# Implementation packages and acceptance plan

## Ground rules

Read the current repo instructions, installed Astro version, route tree, shared UI and current author edits first. Use an isolated branch/worktree. This handoff does not authorize publication, deployment or overwriting hand edits. There is no need to touch SkillMeat infrastructure, credentials or agent runtime policy.

## Packages

### P0-A — Content contract and canonical assets

Owner posture: Evidence Reviewer + Content Engineer.

Map the current six scenes and public receipts into shared data. Resolve all eight exact canonical PNGs. Record hashes/dimensions and inspect mobile text. Reject old substitutes and fake captured evidence. Reconcile each date according to existing research open items; no ad-hoc date repair.

Output: validated thread/evidence/asset data and current manuscript anchor map. No prose flattening or redesign of the thesis taxonomy.

### P0-B — Static essay and focus routes

Owner: UX Implementer.

Implement the selected essay shell, partial-width compositions, section markers, tables, lightweight receipts and WhereThisSits. Add standalone thread, evidence and figure routes using the same records as the inline components. Validate no-JS pages before adding overlays.

Output: correct route content, responsive layouts, real hrefs, relevant titles and canonical metadata.

### P0-C — Inspection controller and return state

Owner: Front-end Architect.

Choose and document one navigation owner. Default is native multipage for this reader route group plus its bounded overlay controller. Preserve modifiers, deep links, direct refresh, Close/Escape and original DOM state. Use one dialog host with logical parent state for thread → evidence/figure.

Output: route-backed overlay, tested root/parent restoration, refresh fallback and safe-history ownership. Do not attach prototype code unmodified next to Astro ClientRouter.

### P0-D — Mobile and accessibility

Owner: Accessibility Reviewer + Implementer.

Add mobile Contents sheet, full-screen Thread/Evidence views and figure inspection. Test focus restoration, tab containment, readable hierarchy, zoom, reduced motion, safe areas and short/landscape viewports.

Output: desktop and mobile states match this spec; no AI assistant, new app tabs or unrequested persistent bottom navigation.

### P1 — Reader context polish

Add authored ContextualNote, dock collapse/hold behavior and subtle active-section styling. Manual choices beat passive scrolling. Defer choreography/animation until the primary experience works. No mandatory auto-advance, scroll-driven gallery or completion checkmarks.

## Tests that must run locally before merging

| ID | Test | Acceptance |
|---|---|---|
| N01 | Essay → Thread → Close | Original paragraph position within 8 CSS px on unchanged layout; original trigger focused |
| N02 | Choose several beats | Underlying essay never scrolls; closing remains one root return |
| N03 | Thread → Figure → Escape | Same thread selection and pane scroll restored |
| N04 | Thread → Evidence → Figure if relevant → return | Parent states and open receipts restored; one active dialog |
| N05 | Browser Back/Forward | Matches owned view history; no double listener or accidental site exit |
| N06 | Copy/open detail URL in a fresh tab | Standalone route works, no false saved-place message |
| N07 | Refresh a focused URL | Correct standalone route, no fake background restoration |
| N08 | Modifier/middle click | Normal new-tab behavior and same target content |
| N09 | No JS | Inline six images, receipt summaries and detail routes remain usable |
| N10 | Navigation or storage unavailable | Fall back to links/in-document inspection; no stuck modal |
| N11 | Back to essay vs Read this scene | Original place versus explicit selected-anchor jump stay distinct |
| N12 | Different viewport or content revision on return | Anchor-relative restoration or honest normal link, no stale-coordinate jump |
| A01 | Keyboard | Initial focus, Tab wrap, Escape and return target correct |
| A02 | Reduced motion | No necessary animation; never passive focus movement |
| A03 | Zoom / 320px / landscape | No page-level horizontal overflow; tables may scroll locally |
| A04 | Screen reader | Correct headings, dialog label, semantic tables and source links |
| C01 | Read marker | Exactly one active article section; does not mean verified/completed |
| C02 | Note selection | One authored note; no unwanted replacement while focused |
| C03 | Collapse and hold | Manual settings persist through scene transitions in the visit |
| C04 | Focus sidebars | Thread: exactly artifact + overview; Evidence: guide + index |
| V01 | Actual canonical art | Correct file/caption/state/format; no stale generated diagram |
| V02 | Content/evidence | No fabricated dates, hashes, versions, metrics, outputs or next essays |
| V03 | Theme | Entry cards absent later; mobile no fake app features |
| V04 | Real manuscript density | Re-run screenshots with final prose and actual fonts/images |

## Visual comparison standard

Use the **rendered v2 screenshot atlas** for layout and state, not the old generated images for text. Compare at identical viewport dimensions. Element hierarchy, pane widths, figure placement, card visibility, line measure, spacing and clipping must match intent; font rendering need not be pixel-identical across operating systems.

Blocking: sidebar components from the wrong mode; hidden/illegible technical claims; invented evidence; incorrect thread order; losing position; no keyboard escape; missing direct routes. Major: density/spacing, oversized revision card, repeated introductory content, mobile overflow. Minor: shadow intensity, subtle corner radius, nonessential ornament.

## What was tested in this environment

See `tests/results.json`. Screenshots and browser-DOM tests run via Chromium with supplied HTML. Managed browser policy prevented navigating to local HTTP/file URLs, so hosted routing and URL-backed Back/Forward tests are **pending**, not passed. In-document dialog fallback, parent/root scroll restoration, basic focus behavior, active markers, content selection and mobile layout can be exercised here.

No production Astro build, Safari, Firefox, iOS device or assistive-technology certification was performed. Do not promote this prototype test result into site release approval.

## Handoff acceptance

Return the proposed diff, resolved asset manifest, screenshot atlas at desktop/mobile widths, actual test results and remaining open items. No publish/merge/deploy without the established author workflow. If a required image/source remains absent, mark that row pending rather than replacing it with plausible art or text.
