src/content/posts/the-registry-wave-agentic-artifact-supply-chain.mdx:218:Name the hops and the question changes shape. **Source:** the repository where the reviewer is authored and the guard was added. **Collection:** the registered set a project deploys from, holding the revision approval attached to. **Project:** the destination that holds a copy and loads it at runtime. Three objects, three separate facts: the revision a project intends to bind, the bytes actually present, and the version a run actually loaded. My checks establish the first two; the third needs a run record. That path is illustrative for one reviewer skill, not a claim that anything I run reconciles all three automatically.
